Error Handling 
     what is it?
          controlling what happens when something goes wrong in your contract.
for eg :
   entering wrong pin :   it shows "Wrong pin entered" message.
   withdraw more than balance : it shows "Insufficient balance"
   ATM is out of cash : "Service unavailable"

without error handling :
   function withdraw(uint amount) public {
    balance -= amount;     //  what if amount > balance? Contract crashes!
    }

with error handling : 
    function withdraw(uint amount) public {
    require(amount <= balance, "Insufficient balance");    // handled!
    balance -= amount;
      }

----------------------
Types of Error Handling
------------------------
       1. require   ----->  check the user input
       2.  revert  ------>  complex conditions
       3.  assert ------> internal bugs

       
1.require :
       checks a condition - if false,stops function and shows error message.
       
 Syntex : 
      require(condition, "error message");

 eg :         
    function deposit(uint amount) public {
    require(amount > 0, "Amount must be greater than 0");
    balance += amount;
}
   when to use :
        * while chcking user input.
        * checking balance.
        * checking permissions.
        * most common error handling method.
-------------------------
2.revert :
     stop functions and reverts all changes - same as require but use if statement.
     
Syntex :
    revert("error message");

    eg : 
       function withdraw(uint amount) public {
    if(amount > balance) {
        revert("Insufficient balance");
    }
    balance -= amount;
      }
   When to use :
    * complex conditions that needs if statement
    * multiple conditions to check.
    * when require syntax is not enough.
  -------------------------------
  3.Assert :
       checks for internal bugs - should never be false.if false - something is seriously wrong.

  Syntex :
       assert(condition);

example :
      function divide(uint a, uint b) public pure returns(uint) {
    assert(b != 0); // b should NEVER be 0
    return a / b;
      }
When to use :
    * check for bugs in your own code.
    * checking invariants.(things that always be true)
    * never for user input checking 

---------------------------------
Custom errors :
    more gas efficient than string error messages.

Syntax :
  // declare custom error
           error InsufficientBalance(uint available, uint required);

// use with revert
           function withdraw(uint amount) public {
                if(amount > balance) {
                       revert InsufficientBalance(balance, amount);
                    }
                  balance -= amount;
            }

Why use custom errors :
    * cheaper gas than string messages.
    * can pass paramaters.
    * more professional.
    * used in real production contracts.
-------------------------------------------------
Example :

// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
pragma solidity ^0.8.0;

contract ErrorHandling {
    uint public balance = 1000;
    bool public isActive = true;

    // custom error
    error InsufficientBalance(uint available, uint required);
    error AccountNotActive();

    // require
    function deposit(uint amount) public {
        require(isActive == true, "Account not active");
        require(amount > 0, "Amount must be greater than 0");
        balance += amount;
    }

    // revert
    function withdraw(uint amount) public {
        if(!isActive) {
            revert AccountNotActive();
        }
        if(amount > balance) {
            revert InsufficientBalance(balance, amount);
        }
        balance -= amount;
    }

    // assert
    function divide(uint a, uint b) public pure returns(uint) {
        assert(b != 0);
        return a / b;
    }
}








       
